WEBVTT

00:00:01.542 --> 00:00:08.185
Look, Brian, those are our motorcycles, David says.

00:00:08.246 --> 00:00:13.659
David and Brian are at Heathrow Airport in London.

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:20.092
They are motorcycle racers from Enfield, a small town in England.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:30.330
They usually race in England and in European countries, but this time they are going to Brazil.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.304
Racers from many countries are going there too.

00:00:35.364 --> 00:00:40.988
They are all going to race across the Amazon jungle.

00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:45.811
Brian is reading a newspaper.

00:00:45.871 --> 00:00:50.294
Listen to this David, he says.

00:00:50.354 --> 00:00:53.606
There's a problem in the Amazon.

00:00:53.666 --> 00:01:00.660
The Indians are very angry because miners are going into the jungle.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:04.561
The miners are taking their homes.

00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:08.724
But David isn't listening to Brian.

00:01:08.784 --> 00:01:13.098
The race is going to be good, he says.

00:01:13.158 --> 00:01:18.442
Yes, and difficult David.

00:01:18.502 --> 00:01:24.006
Two days later, the races are in Brasilia.

00:01:24.066 --> 00:01:27.428
Brian and David are there too.

00:01:27.488 --> 00:01:30.583
A lot of people come and watch.

00:01:30.642 --> 00:01:34.006
It is a beautiful sunny morning.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:36.788
There is a lot of noise.

00:01:36.848 --> 00:01:39.799
People are talking to the races.

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:43.582
Photographers are taking pictures.

00:01:43.642 --> 00:01:48.554
The race is going to start, a young man says.

00:01:48.614 --> 00:01:50.096
Listen.

00:01:50.156 --> 00:01:53.688
Good morning, a man says.

00:01:53.748 --> 00:01:58.518
This is the start of the Amazon rally.

00:01:58.578 --> 00:02:04.447
42 people are going to race from here to my house.

00:02:04.507 --> 00:02:07.258
Are you okay, Brian?

00:02:07.318 --> 00:02:09.329
David asks.

00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:12.450
No, Brian answers.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.591
I've got a problem.

00:02:14.651 --> 00:02:20.973
Look, oil is leaking from the engine of my motorcycle.

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:24.754
Where's that blue for oil leaks?

00:02:24.814 --> 00:02:26.502
Brian asks.

00:02:26.562 --> 00:02:30.032
The racers are putting on their helmets.

00:02:30.092 --> 00:02:34.264
Here, try this, David says.

00:02:34.324 --> 00:02:37.004
He gives Brian some glue.

00:02:37.064 --> 00:02:43.158
Brian puts some glue on his engine, but it comes out very slowly.

00:02:43.218 --> 00:02:49.610
Quickly, Brian, the race is going to start, David says.

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:53.895
But oil is leaking from Brian's engine.

00:02:53.955 --> 00:02:57.870
Quickly, David says again.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.601
The oil stops.

00:03:00.661 --> 00:03:05.924
Brian puts on his helmet and gets on his motorcycle.

00:03:05.984 --> 00:03:11.076
The engines of the motorcycles make a lot of noise.

00:03:11.136 --> 00:03:15.318
The race is starting, David says.

00:03:15.378 --> 00:03:18.550
Let's go, Brian says.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.306
The Amazon Rally starts.

00:03:22.366 --> 00:03:26.224
The first day is okay.

00:03:26.284 --> 00:03:28.704
The roads are good.

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:33.448
The races see many small towns and villages.

00:03:33.508 --> 00:03:37.940
People stand near the road and watch them.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.482
On the second day, the roads are not very good.

00:03:43.542 --> 00:03:50.653
Two Italians, Luigi and Enrico, are in first and second place.

00:03:50.713 --> 00:03:55.672
On the third day, the races are in the jungle.

00:03:55.732 --> 00:03:58.713
The roads are very bad.

00:03:58.773 --> 00:04:03.485
The Brazilians are in first and second place now.

00:04:03.545 --> 00:04:12.148
Then, Camluigi and Enrico, David and Brian, are behind the two Italians.

00:04:12.208 --> 00:04:17.281
The race always stops late in the afternoon.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:25.784
Those Brazilians are very good And they know the road, Brian says that evening.

00:04:25.844 --> 00:04:29.346
The Brazilians aren't a problem.

00:04:29.405 --> 00:04:32.656
The rain is our big problem.

00:04:32.716 --> 00:04:37.478
Look, David answers.

00:04:37.538 --> 00:04:41.469
Day four.

00:04:41.529 --> 00:04:45.391
This is our second day in the jungle.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.771
A difficult day.

00:04:47.831 --> 00:04:50.442
The rain never stops.

00:04:50.502 --> 00:04:53.362
and the road is very bad.

00:04:53.422 --> 00:04:56.673
There are trees across the roads.

00:04:56.733 --> 00:05:02.074
Sometimes we can't stay on our motorcycles.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:08.275
I am first in the race now, and David is second.

00:05:08.335 --> 00:05:11.926
The two Italians are behind us.

00:05:11.986 --> 00:05:15.176
We are happy about that.

00:05:15.236 --> 00:05:21.201
It is seven o'clock now, and it is very dark.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:29.208
The days are very hot in the jungle, but the nights are beautiful.

00:05:29.268 --> 00:05:32.540
David is in bed.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.483
I am going to bed too.

00:05:36.543 --> 00:05:43.168
The race starts very early on the third day in the jungle.

00:05:43.228 --> 00:05:47.661
In the afternoon Brian and David stop.

00:05:47.721 --> 00:05:53.585
The jungle is very beautiful, but they aren't looking at it.

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:58.606
They are looking for the town of Una Una.

00:05:58.666 --> 00:06:01.348
Where are we now?

00:06:01.408 --> 00:06:03.348
Brian asks.

00:06:03.408 --> 00:06:05.620
I don't know.

00:06:05.679 --> 00:06:09.462
Is this the road to Una Una?

00:06:09.521 --> 00:06:13.654
I don't know, David says again.

00:06:13.714 --> 00:06:16.094
Where are the racers?

00:06:16.154 --> 00:06:18.020
Brian asks.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.166
Can you hear them?

00:06:20.226 --> 00:06:23.728
They stop their engines and listen.

00:06:23.787 --> 00:06:26.788
The jungle is quiet.

00:06:26.848 --> 00:06:30.040
Then they hear a noise.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:34.050
Listen, David, Brian says.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.681
What is it?

00:06:35.741 --> 00:06:37.572
David asks.

00:06:37.632 --> 00:06:42.003
It isn't a motorcycle, Brian answers.

00:06:42.063 --> 00:06:45.444
Suddenly they see some men.

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:49.035
They are walking to Brian and David.

00:06:49.094 --> 00:06:53.435
Look at those men, David, Brian says.

00:06:53.495 --> 00:06:55.016
Who are they?

00:06:55.076 --> 00:06:56.966
David asks.

00:06:57.026 --> 00:07:00.327
They aren't racers, David.

00:07:00.387 --> 00:07:04.038
They're Indians.

00:07:04.098 --> 00:07:12.960
The Indians come and talk to Brian and David, but the two young men can't understand them.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:17.512
These Indians are very angry, Brian.

00:07:17.571 --> 00:07:19.308
But why?

00:07:19.368 --> 00:07:20.716
I don't know.

00:07:20.736 --> 00:07:23.958
I can't understand them.

00:07:24.018 --> 00:07:29.182
We've got a problem, Brian," David says.

00:07:29.242 --> 00:07:34.757
The Indians take the two young men to an Indian village.

00:07:34.817 --> 00:07:41.002
A woman with blue eyes comes and talks to Brian and David.

00:07:41.062 --> 00:07:46.016
Her name's Astrid, and she's German.

00:07:46.076 --> 00:07:52.038
She lives in the jungle Because she's working there with the Indians.

00:07:52.097 --> 00:07:54.179
Who are you?

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:56.340
The woman asks.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:01.232
I'm Brian and this is my friend David.

00:08:01.292 --> 00:08:04.254
Why are the Indians angry?

00:08:04.314 --> 00:08:06.426
David asks.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.216
Are you miners?

00:08:09.276 --> 00:08:12.809
The miners want this place.

00:08:12.869 --> 00:08:17.502
Sometimes they come here and they kill the Indians.

00:08:17.562 --> 00:08:19.508
Astrid says.

00:08:19.568 --> 00:08:22.126
We aren't miners.

00:08:22.186 --> 00:08:26.130
We are motorcycle racers, David says.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.922
We want to go to Una Una.

00:08:29.982 --> 00:08:35.276
Astrid talks to Maune, the Indian chief.

00:08:35.336 --> 00:08:39.900
Maune listens and talks to his men.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.013
They aren't angry now.

00:08:43.073 --> 00:08:48.691
The miners are coming to the village, Astrid says.

00:08:48.751 --> 00:08:51.705
Chief Maoni knows that.

00:08:51.766 --> 00:08:55.106
They're going to kill his men.

00:08:55.166 --> 00:08:59.507
Let's get the police, Astrid, Brian says.

00:08:59.567 --> 00:09:00.818
How?

00:09:00.878 --> 00:09:03.248
There's no time.

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:06.399
I can go to Una Una.

00:09:06.459 --> 00:09:10.530
There's a police station there, Brian says.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:15.982
But you don't know the road to Una Una, David says.

00:09:16.042 --> 00:09:20.735
Astrid and Chief Maune talk again.

00:09:20.795 --> 00:09:26.990
Cowak is going to go to Una Una with you tomorrow.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:35.046
He's Chief Maune's son, and he knows the road, Astrid says.

00:09:35.106 --> 00:09:44.226
At seven o'clock in the morning, Brian and Cowak get on Brian's motorcycle.

00:09:44.286 --> 00:09:47.691
Cowak isn't very happy.

00:09:47.751 --> 00:09:51.342
He doesn't know about motorcycles.

00:09:51.402 --> 00:09:54.242
The Indians watch them.

00:09:54.302 --> 00:10:01.044
Brian starts the engine and Cowak gets off the motorcycle quickly.

00:10:01.104 --> 00:10:04.376
The Indians run to the trees.

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:07.676
Astrid talks to Cowak.

00:10:07.736 --> 00:10:11.377
Then he gets on the motorcycle again.

00:10:11.437 --> 00:10:14.782
The Indians watch from the trees.

00:10:14.842 --> 00:10:18.576
Brian starts the engine again.

00:10:18.636 --> 00:10:20.126
Go!

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:21.876
David says.

00:10:21.936 --> 00:10:27.468
Brian and Kawak take the road to Una Una.

00:10:27.528 --> 00:10:36.550
It is difficult in the jungle, but Brian is a good racer and Kawak knows the road.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:41.462
He knows every river and tree in the jungle.

00:10:41.522 --> 00:10:46.614
Early in the afternoon, They come to a big river.

00:10:46.674 --> 00:10:49.697
Brian looks in his roadbook.

00:10:49.757 --> 00:10:53.250
They are near Una Una now.

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:56.772
Then Brian looks at the engine.

00:10:56.832 --> 00:10:58.954
Oh no!

00:10:59.014 --> 00:11:03.758
Oil is leaking from the engine again, he thinks.

00:11:03.818 --> 00:11:06.880
He stops the motorcycle.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:09.982
I haven't got any glue.

00:11:10.042 --> 00:11:13.678
Where's David's glue, he thinks.

00:11:13.738 --> 00:11:18.122
This time, I've got a big problem.

00:11:18.182 --> 00:11:21.824
Cowak looks at the oil.

00:11:21.884 --> 00:11:26.935
Then he walks to a tree and takes a green fruit.

00:11:26.996 --> 00:11:30.748
He puts the fruit on the hot engine.

00:11:30.808 --> 00:11:33.798
The leak stops.

00:11:33.858 --> 00:11:37.810
That's very good, Brian says.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:40.102
Thank you, Cowak.

00:11:40.161 --> 00:11:42.232
Let's go.

00:11:42.292 --> 00:11:45.602
They start to drive again.

00:11:45.662 --> 00:11:53.754
The oil often leaks from the engine, but Kalak stops it with the green fruit every time.

00:11:53.814 --> 00:11:58.156
They arrive in Una Una in the evening.

00:11:58.216 --> 00:12:05.418
They meet Captain Silver at the police station, and Brian talks to him.

00:12:05.478 --> 00:12:08.908
The miners are coming, Captain.

00:12:08.968 --> 00:12:13.278
They're going to kill the Indians, Brian says.

00:12:13.338 --> 00:12:16.199
You're right, young man.

00:12:16.259 --> 00:12:18.870
We don't have much time.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:22.181
Captain Silver talks to a policeman.

00:12:22.241 --> 00:12:25.102
Let's go to the Indian village.

00:12:25.162 --> 00:12:27.153
I want 20 men.

00:12:27.213 --> 00:12:29.224
Quickly.

00:12:29.284 --> 00:12:34.636
They get to the Indian village late in the afternoon.

00:12:34.696 --> 00:12:39.328
Let's wait for the miners, Captain Silver says.

00:12:39.388 --> 00:12:42.372
Go behind the trees.

00:12:42.432 --> 00:12:44.867
It's night again.

00:12:44.927 --> 00:12:48.400
They are all waiting for the miners.

00:12:48.459 --> 00:12:50.100
Look!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:54.262
Captain Silver says, they're coming!

00:12:54.322 --> 00:12:57.825
The miners are coming from the jungle.

00:12:57.885 --> 00:13:01.058
They're moving very quietly.

00:13:01.118 --> 00:13:04.840
There are a lot of miners in the village now.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:07.902
They are looking for the Indians.

00:13:07.962 --> 00:13:11.192
The village is quiet.

00:13:11.252 --> 00:13:17.132
Then Captain Silver says, This is Captain Silver!

00:13:17.192 --> 00:13:19.114
Don't move!

00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:23.486
The miners run, and the Indians run too.

00:13:23.546 --> 00:13:26.268
They make a lot of noise.

00:13:26.328 --> 00:13:30.730
Two miners find David and catch him.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:34.931
They're going to kill me, David thinks.

00:13:34.992 --> 00:13:38.964
But then two policemen run to him.

00:13:39.024 --> 00:13:41.233
Stop, they say.

00:13:41.293 --> 00:13:44.512
We are policemen."

00:13:44.572 --> 00:13:51.574
In the morning, Chief Maune and his people are very happy.

00:13:51.634 --> 00:13:55.334
A lot of Indians are dancing.

00:13:55.394 --> 00:14:01.196
Chief Maune has two beautiful necklaces in his hands.

00:14:01.256 --> 00:14:07.910
He smiles and gives a red necklace to David.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:14.576
He's giving you an Indian name, Astrid says.

00:14:14.636 --> 00:14:19.038
Jaguari is a small jaguar.

00:14:19.098 --> 00:14:24.980
Then Chief Maune gives a black necklace to Brian.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:28.440
Manui, he says.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:32.732
Quick runner, Astrid says.

00:14:32.792 --> 00:14:37.674
Brian gives his helmet to Kawak.

00:14:37.734 --> 00:14:40.882
Champion, he says.

00:14:40.942 --> 00:14:44.050
They all smile.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:49.703
Captain Silver takes Brian and David to Manaus.

00:14:49.763 --> 00:14:52.054
The racers are there.

00:14:52.114 --> 00:14:54.876
They are photographers too.

00:14:54.936 --> 00:15:02.610
They are taking pictures of the champions, Luigi and Enrico, the two Italians.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:06.582
Brian, David, hello.

00:15:06.642 --> 00:15:09.458
Enrico says, look.

00:15:09.518 --> 00:15:13.144
We are the champions, Luigi says.

00:15:13.204 --> 00:15:17.366
Congratulations, Brian and David say.

00:15:17.426 --> 00:15:19.248
Are you okay?

00:15:19.308 --> 00:15:21.098
Enrico asks.

00:15:21.158 --> 00:15:24.842
Now we are, Brian says.

00:15:24.902 --> 00:15:32.486
Brian and David's talk to Enrico and Luigi about the Indians and the miners.

00:15:32.546 --> 00:15:36.846
You're champions too, Luigi says.

00:15:36.906 --> 00:15:45.088
Yes, they're champions of a very important race, Captain Silver says.

00:15:45.148 --> 00:15:49.820
Brian and David look at their Indian necklaces.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:55.612
Congratulations, Manway, David says to his friend.

00:15:55.672 --> 00:16:00.245
Congratulations, Jagwari, Brian says.

